# cp users.txt.example users.txt   (users.txt is git-ignored)
#
# People who get access to every cluster. Edit this whenever someone sends
# you their public IP and SSH public key, then run ./up.sh - it takes about a
# minute when the clusters already exist. Delete a line to revoke access.
#
#   name    lowercase, used as their Kubernetes and SSH user name
#   role    admin = cluster-admin | edit = change workloads | view = read-only
#   ip      their public IP (or CIDR); several: 1.2.3.4,5.6.7.8
#   key     their SSH public key (the whole line from their ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub)
#
# name     role    ip               key
# alice    admin   203.0.113.10     ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... alice@laptop
# bob      admin   198.51.100.7     ssh-rsa AAAAB3NzaC1yc2EAAAADAQABAAAB... bob@desktop
